course: dictionary
lesson: 13468
title: Hurting: pain, injury, or feelings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word hurting has three meanings. It can mean causing pain or injury: «You are hurting me!» It can mean feeling pain: «My knee is hurting.» It can also mean upsetting someone's feelings: «Her unkind words were hurting her.»
explain: Use the context to choose the right meaning. If someone is pushing you, hurting means causing pain. If your leg aches after a fall, hurting means feeling pain. If someone is sad after an unkind comment, hurting means upsetting their feelings.
explain: Hurting can be about the body or about feelings. Unkind words can be hurting just as much as a hit. If something is hurting you, or someone is hurting you or another child, tell an adult you trust.
fact: Hurting means causing pain or injury, feeling pain, or upsetting someone's feelings.
fact: «You are hurting me!» means that someone's action is causing you pain.
fact: «My knee is hurting.» means your knee feels pain.
fact: «Hurting someone's feelings» means making them sad or upset with words or actions.
fact: Hurting others, even as a joke, is not OK. Tell an adult if someone is hurting you or another child.
exercise: «Stop hurting me!» What does hurting mean here? | Sleeping quietly | Feeling happy | Singing loudly | *Causing pain
exercise: «My ankle is hurting after the fall.» What does hurting mean here? | Running very fast | Making someone laugh | Painting a picture | *Feeling pain
exercise: Sam says, «Calling her names was hurting her feelings.» What does hurting mean here? | *Upsetting her | Making her dinner | Helping her to read | Giving her a present
test: «Ali's sharp words were hurting Maya.» What might hurting mean here? | Making Maya laugh | Lifting Maya up | Making Maya's bed | *Upsetting Maya's feelings
test: Which sentence is about feeling pain? | Ben is pushing his friend in the line | Ben is hitting the ball hard | *Ben's arm is hurting after he fell
exam: «If someone is hurting you, what should you do?» | Ignore it and hope it stops | Keep it to yourself forever | Hurt them back | *Tell an adult you trust
